Moving a plate. A translation is a placement and reuses the shape (plan.rs test at 2296-2312).
A rewrite to a new outline adds that outline once: z2 cells4 goes from 734 to 1468 segments, not 1,073,108.
Only if every row had its own outline would a plate reach the handoff's figure: 731 x 734 = 536554.

Point motion on z2 cells4, baked into f32 records as a point write would be (a mirror, on one frame)
  translation by (0.37, -0.11): 1 distinct outlines of 731; about 734 new segments a frame
  uniform scale by 0.93 about the origin: 1 distinct outlines of 731; about 734 new segments a frame
  rotation by 0.1 rad: 731 distinct outlines of 731; about 536554 new segments a frame
  a warp, y + 0.01 sin(3x + 2y): 731 distinct outlines of 731; about 536554 new segments a frame
  all rows distinct: first motion frame 536554 + 536554 = 1073108 against 1<<20 = 1048576: refused by name, nothing unreachable yet
  with max_retained_segments raised: 536554 unreachable > max_unreachable_segments 65536, so a rebuild on every later frame
  and at the 4-a-segment bound 4292432 pieces against MonoTable's fixed 1<<22 = 4194304, which RenderOptions cannot change

Monotone table. fill.rs build_with_limits walks plan.shapes().shapes(), once an outline (fill.rs:594-603).
z2 cells4: at most 4 x 734 = 2936 pieces, not 2,146,216; about 137 KiB at the handoff's 48 B a piece, not 98 MiB
Sharing shrinks the table only. Raster still walks each instance, so it does not lower the raster estimate.

